====Adjective====
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[present|Present]]; [[current]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=17th century|author=w:Joseph Glanvill|title=Scepsis Scientifica: Or, Confest Ignorance, the Way to Science; in an Essay of the Vanity of Dogmatizing and Confident Opinion|year_published=1885|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=3jU0AQAAMAAJ&q=%22Our+now+happiness%22+Glanvill&dq=%22Our+now+happiness%22+Glanvill&hl=en&sa=X&ei=WSHqUbm2MsXqiAeS3YCwBQ&redir_esc=y|page=207|passage=Defects seem as necessary to our '''now''' happiness as their Opposites.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1855|author=Conrad Swackhamer|title=The United States democratic review|volume=5|passage=The history of the infant colonies teaches us that the country comprised within the limits of the '''now''' United States of America was originally patented in the reign of James I., of England, into ''two portions:'' that in less than eighty years from that period, the same was again divided into ''twelve'' distinct provinces; a ''thirteenth'' being after added in the creation of the State of Georgia.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1908|title=The English reports|passage=Where in assumpsit for money lent, the defendant pleaded that in an action in which the '''now''' defendant was plaintiff, and the '''now''' plaintiff was defendant,{{...}}.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2010 March 17|work=w:The Daily Telegraph|url=http://www.telegraph.co.uk/culture/tvandradio/bbc/7457761/Radio-4-apologises-for-day-old-shipping-forecast.html|title=Radio 4 apologises for day old shipping forecast|passage=Radio 4's continuity announcer said at the end of the show: "As many of you will have noticed, that edition of The Now Show wasn't very '''now'''. It was actually last week's programme. Our apologies for that."}}
# {{lb|en|informal}} [[fashionable|Fashionable]]; [[popular]]; [[up to date]]; [[current]].
#: {{ux|en|I think this band's sound is very '''now'''.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|medium=television production|year=2000|title=Black Books|episode=Cooking the Books|number=1|season=1|passage=Bernard: What does it do?</br>Fran: It's very in.</br>Bernard: You don't know what it is, do you?</br>Fran: It's very '''now'''.}}
# {{lb|en|archaic|legal}} At the time the [[will]] is written. Used in order to prevent any [[inheritance]] from being transferred to a person of a future marriage. Does not indicate the existence of a previous marriage.
#: {{ux|en|'''Now''' wife.}}

